// REJECTED — the provide-method twin of the fn-body index-type refusal
// (roadmap item 404, sibling of item 392). A `List` index must be an `Int`; a
// bare `fn`/`test` body (stratum 1, `infer_ast`) refuses `xs[s]` where `s: Str`,
// but the SAME expression inside a `provide` method body was lowered through a
// different stratum (`_lower_component_pure_expr` + `infer_ir`) that ran the
// type oracle only in its NON-raising mode, so it compiled clean — the same
// context-scoping gap item 392 closed for the Any-field-read.
//
// item 404 routes the provide-method body through the SAME raising oracle the
// activation-setup body and the `fn`/`test` bodies use (the `_sweep` mirror), so
// a definite operator / index / builtin misuse now fires uniformly wherever the
// expression sits.
//
// expected error:
//   index expects `Int`, got `Str`

service Reader {
  fn read(s: Str) -> Int
}

component Parser provides reader: Reader {
  provide reader {
    fn read(s) {
      let xs: List[Int] = [1, 2, 3]
      let n = xs[s]
      return n
    }
  }
}
